{"id": "EUVD-2026-93150", "enisaUuid": "ebbd9940-c721-3d8b-b9ce-6a9bcddc7a5f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nKEYS: encrypted: fix integer overflow of datablob_len\n\nencrypted_key_alloc() stores datablob_len in a u16. It is computed from\nmultiple string and payload lengths. If the result exceeds U16_MAX, the\nassignment truncates the allocation size. KASAN reports a 32760-byte\nslab-out-of-bounds write when __ekey_init() copies the master key\ndescription into the undersized buffer.\n\nThe total payload length stored in key->datalen is also a u16. Use\ncheck_add_overflow() to reject values that do not fit either destination,\nand use kzalloc_flex() for the flexible-array allocation.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:44:57", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:15:54", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1e720f63dbafc093a8f5d519f05b67724993edd4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a1a98eca102b1cbbc37ff9eaa197ae4e6a3ea4b0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cca38f2102a4cd35eda8d48950df4817b4b24757", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8697c431e297eb0d0ab13dda6bc172b48a34f05c"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98222", "GHSA-8jg9-f732-244h"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "13ee6b22-8d38-3119-8f73-c991c1c63d4a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7e70cb4978507cf31d76b90e4cfb4c28cad87f0c <8697c431e297eb0d0ab13dda6bc172b48a34f05c"}, {"id": "40a136f1-5145-362e-a64f-3aace8eb5983", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "6ed94f0f-b4f5-358c-b7b4-49fff65db2d2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "8c3f09e9-0a1a-3a58-a208-3dd13db5e9fc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7e70cb4978507cf31d76b90e4cfb4c28cad87f0c <1e720f63dbafc093a8f5d519f05b67724993edd4"}, {"id": "9157b8